  "final_message": "I put `channel` back everywhere I removed it, but I couldn't run the tests, typecheck or arch check to confirm. The shell command that would have run them was blocked because no one was available to approve it. So I haven't confirmed CI is green.\n\nThe CI failure showed that my earlier premise was wrong. `analytics-ingest` has a contract (ARCH-4) that requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. So something does read the field, even though nothing in this repo does. That contract lives outside this repo (I found no `ARCH-4` or `analytics-ingest` text in it), so I couldn't edit it.\n\nI did the revert by hand with the edit tool, since a bulk `git checkout` would have needed the same approval:\n- **Source:** `channel` is back on `Order`, `NewOrder` and `OrderPlaced`. `src/core/order.ts` has its `CHANNELS` list and validation again, `src/core/events.ts` emits `channel`, and `src/api/requestParsing.ts` reads it.\n- **Tests and docs:** the fixtures, the validation test, and the `createApp` examples in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are restored.\n\nPlease run `git diff` to check that nothing is left over from the removal. Then run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run arch`.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to drop it from its contract first. Once that's done and nothing else depends on it, the removal can be redone. Because it's a breaking change to the event, bump `schemaVersion` to 4 at that point.",
